<title>HONG KONG: Hongkong Bank appoints chief economist.</title>
<headline>Hongkong Bank appoints chief economist.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corp has appointed Jan Lee as chief economist effective from July 1, the bank said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Lee currently is managing director of Nava Securities in Singapore, the statement said.</p>
<p>He previously worked as a senior economist with the Australian government and with a number of banking groups, including Union Bank of Switzerland, W.I. Carr and Goldman Sachs, it said.</p>
<p>Hongkong Bank is a unit of HSBC Holdings Plc.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
